{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you shall take.</b> Now he explains how they would take from the blood and put it on the lintel." "The word אגודת is like חבורה (a binding), as in ויהיו לאגדה אחד (II Samuel 2:25). Rabbi Marinus said that the alef is added and it is from the root גדוד, and others said that the alef is a root letter, as in וחשב אפודתו (Exodus 28:8 below)." "The Gaon [Saadia] explained ezov in Arabic as za'atar, and in the foreign tongue as origanum, and it is a distinguished herb among seasonings. This is impossible, for Scripture says of ezov that which grows out of the wall (I Kings 5:13), and I do not know what it is; only by reason it is not a hardy plant, for it is the opposite of the cedar that the verse mentions." "Some say that the Pesach was slaughtered at the threshold of the gate, and they dipped the ezov in it and reached the doorposts, as in וימד סף השער (Ezekiel 40:6), אמות הספים (Isaiah 6). Others said that it is a vessel upon which they slaughtered, as in משכב וספות (II Samuel 17:25)." "And I will further explain until morning."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {3 "II Samuel 17:25 in standard chapter divisions does not contain משכב וספות; this citation may refer to a different verse or reflect a variant numbering; the phrase appears in II Samuel 17:28."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:48.029382687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}